      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© Georg Thieme Verlag KG Stuttgart · New York.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "Compare the efficacy and tolerability of oral spray formulations delivering 2.5, 5, and 10\u2009mg ambroxol (AXS) per application (4 actuations/application) in relieving acute sore throat vs. spraying a matched placebo solution."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "DESIGN",
            "content": "Multi-centre, placebo-controlled, randomised, double-blind trial with up to 6 daily applications of the assigned medication for up to 3 days."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PATIENTS",
            "content": "511 outpatients with acute sore throat were enrolled, 494 were treated."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "TREATMENTS",
            "content": "Up to 6 spray applications per day as needed for up to 3 days."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "RESULTS",
            "content": "All treatments led to a reduction in pain intensity (PI); the mean cumulative PI-reductions over the first 2\u2009h after the 1(st) dose (SPIDnorm(0-2)) were 24.7, 26.6, 26.0, and 32.2% (SEM: 0.023) of the predose PI for treatment with placebo, and the 2.5, 5, and 10\u2009mg AXS, respectively. These mean reductions were 2 (CI: -3.6; 7.5), 1.3 (CI: -4.3; 6.8), and 7.5 (CI: 2.0;13.1) percent points larger than for placebo. The 2.5 and 5\u2009mg AXS were not distinguishable from placebo, but the 10\u2009mg AXS was evidently superior. The numbers needed to treat (NNT) when comparing 10\u2009mg AXS with placebo, were 9.5 and 8.8 for an average pain relief of 33 and 50% of the maximum achievable effect over the first 2\u2009h."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "10\u2009mg AXS showed a statistically significantly superior pain reduction relative to the placebo spray. Treatment with 10\u2009mg AXS reaches an extent of pain relief that can be accepted to be clinically meaningful and was well tolerated."
          }
        ]
      },
